# Documented risk acceptance — reviewed 2026-08-13, aegis-api:ci image.
# Every entry here has a released fix (so `ignore-unfixed: true` in ci.yml
# doesn't already exclude it); each is skipped for a specific, checked
# reason below, not blanket-suppressed. Re-run `trivy image --severity
# HIGH,CRITICAL aegis-api:ci` without this file to see the full raw list.

# --- mlflow: fix requires the 3.x major line ---
# All fixed versions below are mlflow>=3.0 (we're pinned to 2.22.4). The
# vulnerable code paths are in the MLflow TRACKING SERVER (model-serving
# RCE, artifact-handler path traversal, auth bypass, SSRF, temp-file/
# credential handling) — that server runs in the separate `mlflow`
# container (ghcr.io/mlflow/mlflow:v2.22.0), not in aegis-api. This image
# only has the mlflow *client* library installed (mlflow.set_tracking_uri,
# mlflow.sklearn.load_model) for MODEL_SOURCE=registry — it never runs
# `mlflow server`, so these request-handler vulnerabilities have no
# reachable code path here. Upgrading to mlflow 3.x untested this late
# risks breaking the Model Registry integration verified working in
# task 8.7 (mlflow.sklearn.log_model signature, MlflowClient API changed
# between 2.x and 3.x) — deferred as a follow-up, not silently dropped.
CVE-2025-15036
CVE-2025-15379
CVE-2026-0596
CVE-2026-2635
CVE-2026-2651
CVE-2026-4035
CVE-2025-10279
CVE-2025-14279
CVE-2025-14287
CVE-2025-15031
CVE-2026-2033
CVE-2026-2393
CVE-2026-2614
CVE-2026-2652
CVE-2026-4137
# CVE-2026-8147 (trace-endpoint auth-bypass, CVSS 8.1): requires
# `mlflow server` running WITH auth enabled. aegis-api runs only the
# client lib (set_tracking_uri / sklearn.load_model / MlflowClient);
# the deployed mlflow server container runs without auth flags. Neither
# surface is reachable -> CVSS Environmental ≈ 0. Fixed in 3.14.0
# (NVD/OSV); folds into the mlflow-3.x upgrade follow-up above.
CVE-2026-8147

# --- pyarrow: transitive via datasets==3.6.0, fix needs a major bump ---
# 19.0.1 -> 23.0.1 is outside the range datasets==3.6.0 was tested
# against; the CVE is a DoS (use-after-free) in Arrow's C++ engine, not
# a code-execution path reachable from our API surface.
CVE-2026-25087

# --- starlette: transitive via fastapi==0.121.2, fix needs 0.x -> 1.x ---
# CVE-2026-54283 (form() limits DoS): fastapi pins starlette in its own
# compatible range; bumping independently risks breaking fastapi's request
# handling untested this late.
# CVE-2026-48818 (StaticFiles UNC-path SSRF/credential theft): Windows-only
# attack vector (UNC paths, \\server\share) — this image runs on Linux
# (python:3.11-slim), where UNC paths aren't a meaningful OS concept, so
# this specific CVE has no exploitable path in this deployment regardless.
CVE-2026-54283
CVE-2026-48818

# --- build-time-only tooling, never invoked by API request handling ---
# wheel 0.45.1: a leftover copy from pip's build-isolation step (we pin
# wheel==0.46.2 in requirements.txt; this is a second, vendored instance),
# not the one used to install our dependencies at runtime.
CVE-2026-24049
# jaraco.context 5.3.0: vendored inside setuptools/_vendor/, a build-time
# packaging dependency — the path-traversal-via-tar-archive CVE requires
# calling jaraco.context's tar extraction, which nothing in aegis-api does.
CVE-2026-23949
